response:
Individuals who are not qualified to avail of the 8% income tax rate include: 

a) Purely compensation income earners;

b) VAT-registered taxpayers, regardless of gross sales/receipts;

c) Non-VAT taxpayers whose gross sales/receipts exceeded ₱3,000,000;

d) Taxpayers subject to Other Percentage Taxes under Title V of the Tax Code, except those under Section 116;

e) Partners of a General Professional Partnership (GPP);

f) Individuals enjoying income tax exemption, such as those registered under the Barangay Micro Business Enterprises (BMBEs) [S1]. 

Please verify with a CPA or your RDO.
